-- A language tag that nothing backs. The rule has no other wording, no `@lang`
-- line declares `the`, and no name has a wording in `the` beside one in another
-- language, so `the` is almost certainly the first word of the sentence and not
-- a language. The wording is attached either way; the diagnostic says what to
-- write.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `over limit` @nlg:the claim of %amount% is over the limit
  IF amount GREATER THAN 100
